      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Occupational asthma is defined as \"a disease of variable airflow limitations and/or airway hyper-responsiveness due to causes and conditions attributable to a particular occupational environment and not stimuli that are being encountered outside the workplace.\" An analysis of general population-based studies published up to 2007 showed that 17.6% of all adult-onset asthma is due to workplace exposures. In this article, Different aspects of occupational asthma are briefly reviewed."},
